{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":627411,"ns":0,"title":"Jewel bearing","extract":"A jewel bearing is a plain bearing in which a metal spindle turns in a jewel-lined pivot hole.  The hole is typically shaped like a torus and is slightly larger than the shaft diameter.","description":"Jewel-lined bearing used in precision instruments, particularly mechanical watches","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}